      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is Yan Qing, the same young East Asian man as Picture 1: same face, black hair, small scar above the outer end of his left eyebrow, plain dark casual clothes. He begins frame-left on the customer side, receives the pork parcel with both hands, turns toward the bicycle at frame-left, and stays beside that bicycle. He never crosses behind the counter or moves to frame right.\n<Subject 2> is the same stocky middle-aged butcher in Picture 1, wearing the same navy work shirt and worn brown apron. He stays behind the counter on frame right. After releasing the parcel he lowers his hands and remains there; he does not follow the customer.\n<Subject 3> is the one dark blue-black step-through electric bicycle from Picture 1, with the same headlamp, handlebar, seat, wheel shape and rear rack. It remains parked in the aisle at frame left and does not roll or change orientation.\n<Subject 4> is the same single large kraft-wrapped pork parcel passed between them in Picture 1. Keep the same size, shape, paper folds and visible paper marks. Do not split it or create another parcel.\n<Picture 1> fixes the camera, the two faces, wardrobe, market geometry, lighting, screen direction, bike design and starting hand positions.\n\nsummary:\nOne static medium-wide shot shows a single practical action: Yan Qing receives the wrapped parcel, turns to the nearby e-bike and secures that same parcel flat on its rear rack. The butcher remains behind the counter. Yan Qing does not ride away in this shot.\n\nretention_analysis:\nKeep both identities, faces, hair, clothing and screen sides stable. Preserve the same market aisle and stall anchors. The one bicycle remains parked at frame left. The one parcel remains the same parcel from the prior shot. Only Yan Qing moves from the counter toward the nearby bicycle; the butcher stays on frame right. No camera move, zoom, cut, axis crossing, duplication, extra prop or extra person.\n\ndetailed_description:\nPhotorealistic live-action drama, matching Picture 1 and the preceding shot's natural market look. Static eye-level medium-wide side-three-quarter camera from the established aisle side. Keep the counter and stall on frame right and the customer aisle/bicycle on frame left. Practical warm market lamps with faint cool first-light ambience; damp floor, realistic fabric and paper. This is a candid narrative action, not a commercial product shot. The parcel lies lengthwise and balanced on the rear rack behind the seat, not on the handlebar or front wheel.\n\nOne uninterrupted 7.29-second action:\n0.0-1.0s The butcher releases the parcel; Yan Qing takes its full weight with both hands. The parcel stays one rigid paper-wrapped bundle.\n1.0-2.7s Yan Qing turns toward frame left and takes two or three short careful steps to the bicycle. The camera remains completely still. The butcher stays behind the counter.\n2.7-4.5s Yan Qing lowers the parcel flat and lengthwise onto the rear rack behind the seat, keeping it centered and clear of both wheels.\n4.5-6.6s He pulls one plain dark elastic cargo strap from the rack over the parcel and secures it to the rack sides. The single strap is functional and unbranded; no extra bags appear.\n6.6-7.29s Yan Qing presses the parcel once to confirm it is secure, then holds beside the parked bicycle. The bicycle stays still; no mounting or riding yet.\n\nNo subtitles, captions, readable signs, logos, watermarks or app UI. No added dialogue is needed for this visual shot; audio is not being evaluated. No advertising pose, no camera-facing presentation, no package duplication, no changed bicycle, no face or clothing changes, no extra people, no movement behind the counter, no wheel rotation, no riding away, no cartoon, illustration or flat 3D look.",
